\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VII}{\ignorespaces Cross-dataset behaviour of the operator at the released HybridGL operating point. The three splits differ sharply, and for construction reasons, in how often an expression carries a spatial relation: RefCOCO$+$ was collected with location words excluded. ``$\Delta $ fired'' is the delta restricted to expressions whose returned index the operator changed. Wrong-instance share is the fraction of the oracle gap mass that class carries.}}{7}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cross}{{VII}{7}{Cross-dataset behaviour of the operator at the released HybridGL operating point. The three splits differ sharply, and for construction reasons, in how often an expression carries a spatial relation: RefCOCO$+$ was collected with location words excluded. ``$\dD $ fired'' is the delta restricted to expressions whose returned index the operator changed. Wrong-instance share is the fraction of the oracle gap mass that class carries}{table.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a) The operator's benefit tracks how often expressions carry a spatial relation. Filled markers: all expressions; hollow diamonds: the spatial stratum only. The RefCOCO$+$ outcome was predicted before the run, from the dataset's construction. (b) Deltas by relation type on RefCOCO. Ordinal and relation-free expressions are unchanged by construction.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dose}{{2}{7}{(a) The operator's benefit tracks how often expressions carry a spatial relation. Filled markers: all expressions; hollow diamonds: the spatial stratum only. The RefCOCO$+$ outcome was predicted before the run, from the dataset's construction. (b) Deltas by relation type on RefCOCO. Ordinal and relation-free expressions are unchanged by construction}{figure.2}{}}
